## Lessons From weatherman12's Approach

Traders studying weatherman12's methodology can extract several principles worth considering. First, win rate is not the only metric that matters, and in some strategies, it barely matters at all. Profitability depends on the product of win rate and average win size minus the product of loss rate and average loss size. A trader winning half their bets can generate outsized returns if position sizing and conviction alignment are properly calibrated. weatherman12's results demonstrate this mathematical reality in practice.

Second, selectivity has value. With only 21 markets traded, weatherman12 has clearly passed on countless opportunities that did not meet their criteria. This discipline prevents the dilution of capital and attention across marginal setups. Third, the early mover advantage requires accepting uncertainty. Markets reward traders who act before consensus forms, but that timing inherently means operating with incomplete information. weatherman12's profile suggests a comfort with this tradeoff that many traders never develop. These patterns become visible when you track how the [top 50 Polymarket traders](/best-polymarket-traders-to-follow-2026/) actually behave rather than how conventional wisdom suggests they should behave.

